In article <15119.28ece2ba@ecs.umass.edu> daly@ecs.umass.edu (Bryon Daly, ECE dept, UMass, Amherst) writes:
>Hello, I'm looking for a few hints, solutions on how to avoid starving early
>on in the game.
>
>I'd appreciate any pointers, cheats, whatever, to solve this problem, or make
>it a less pressing concern.

** Possible food spoilers **

There's one way that will almost guarantee that you will never starve:
#pray to your God whenever you get really hungry. Simply wait until
you are weak, or better yet, wait until you start fainting, and then
just #pray. This should always work, and your God will nourish your
stomach. Just make sure that you don't pray too often (i.e. only pray
when you're about to die) and don't do anything to make your God
pissed off at you, like killing peaceful monsters, etc.

Also, wearing rings and amulets increase your food consumption, so don't wear
then unless you are currently using their ability.

>How do people accumulate enough food to actually spare some to train their pet?

Well, I generally only give my pet tripe, which isn't good for players
to eat. Note that your pet tends to eat lots of the corpses monsters
leave, so you might want to abandon your pet in a closed room unless
you want his fighting ability. (Although if you leave him for a while
and then go back to the room he's in, he might attack you since he's
hungry.)

